{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.pair_count_exceeds_adjacency_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.pair_count_exceeds_adjacency_budget","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L150-L167","doc":"**The layout-free bound**, which survives dropping contiguity. A linear\narrangement of `3A` strands has only `3A-1` adjacent position pairs, and each\ncan carry at most one nucleon pair, so no layout whatever realises the complete\ncoupling once `C(A,2) > 3A-1` — that is, from `A = 7`, which is `⁷Li`.\n\nStated without division as `2·(3A-1) < A·(A-1)`. At `A = 7` this is `40 < 42`;\nthe exhaustive search in the probe agrees, finding witnesses for `A = 2 … 6` and\nnone at `A = 7`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.pair_count_exceeds_path_for_three_or_more","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.pair_count_exceeds_path_for_three_or_more","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L140-L148","doc":"The counting gap the theorem above expresses: a contiguous layout supplies\n`A-1` couplings (the path), and the all-pairs coupling needs `C(A,2)`. Stated\nwithout division as `2·(A-1) < A·(A-1)`, which is the same inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.complete_coupling_forces_A_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.complete_coupling_forces_A_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L125-L138","doc":"**The binding producer's coupling is unreachable.** If every pair of the `A`\nnucleons is coupled — which is exactly what `_step_chain_generic` emits, one\ninter-nucleon letter per (new nucleon, earlier nucleon) pair — then `A ≤ 2`.\n\nSo the deuteron re-embeds and nothing above it does: at `A = 2` the single pair\n`{0,1}` IS the one adjacency, while from `A = 3` the pair `{0,2}` has no\ngenerator to sit on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.coupled_forces_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.coupled_forces_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L109-L123","doc":"Coupled nucleons are adjacent in the layout order — the coupling graph of a\ncontiguous `3A` layout is contained in the **path** `P_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.Coupled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.Coupled","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L105-L107","doc":"The unordered coupling relation: nucleons `i` and `j` are coupled when some\ngenerator crosses a strand of one with a strand of the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.no_coupling_of_gap_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.no_coupling_of_gap_two","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L92-L103","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form the counting argument uses: nucleons two or more\napart admit **no** single-generator coupling, in either direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.coupling_forces_consecutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.coupling_forces_consecutive","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L80-L90","doc":"**The obstruction.** A single generator can only couple CONSECUTIVE\nnucleons: a generator crosses two adjacent strands, blocks are three wide, so\nreaching from nucleon `i` into a nucleon above it lands in `i+1` and nowhere\nfurther.\n\nEverything else in this file is arithmetic on top of this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.IsCoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.IsCoupling","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L70-L78","doc":"`x` is the lower endpoint of a single-generator coupling between nucleons\n`i` and `j`: the generator `σ_x` crosses strands `x` and `x+1`, so a coupling\nputs `x` in nucleon `i` and `x+1` in nucleon `j`.\n\nThis is `LayoutConflict.IsCoupling` with the second nucleon left FREE rather\nthan fixed to `i+1` — which is the whole point, since the binding word needs\ncouplings between nucleons that are not neighbours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.nucleonBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.nucleonBlock","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L66-L68","doc":"Nucleon `k`'s three strands in the canonical `atom_braid_word_3A` layout:\npositions `3k`, `3k+1`, `3k+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.mem_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.mem_block","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ContiguousCouplingGraph.block","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ContiguousCouplingGraph.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The block of `C` consecutive strand positions starting at `p`. Same shape as\n`LayoutConflict.block`; restated so this file stands alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}